==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Totem Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Acrobat Cats''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Stilts Cat can regain terrain against short ranged, bulky Angels like [[Divine Cyclone]] quite effectively. Since it lacks area attacks and angels tend to come in groups, or outrange it, or be easy to push back with damage, better results can usually be expected from other stallers. Despite this, the first two forms can be used to cheese Divine Cyclone's stage if you have a stack.

==='''True Form'''===
Acrobat Cats are both a lot bulkier and have a more consistent knockback chance. Despite this, their usability barely changes, mainly due to the lack of area attacks. Still, they work well with [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]], as they can relieve the pressure by knocking back some of the enemies, plus they make it harder for them to advance through temporary gaps. They can also stun-lock a [[Sunfish Jones]] who is set as boss or save the base from [[Boraphim]].

==='''Talents'''===
The most notable Talents are [[Surge Attack]] and immunity to [[Wave Attack]]s. The former fixes the single target issue at the cost of not happening every attack; it allows Acrobat to seriously get in the way of incoming angels, using other traits to generate their surges often. When combined with wave immunity, [[Angelic Beast Rajakong]] and [[Youcan]] may seriously struggle to spawn any waves, plus the ability would allow for their use in stages where waves can't be prevented. Wave immunity also turns them into a decent wave immune ranged meatshield, although they face competitions from [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Dread Pirate Catley]].

Attack up is inconsequential, but health up can sometimes help. Freeze resist is rarely going to help too, so it should be unlocked only if a situation demands it.

==='''Orb'''===
Defence up against angels is the best option. Note that it won't come into play much either way, so saving your orbs is recommended.

